  Proprietary and confidential.

  MAM video proxy configuration.

  Stock nuxeo-platform-video (video-service-contrib.xml) enables THREE
  automatic proxy transcodes on every uploaded video: "MP4 480p"
  (H.264 / libx264, fast), "WebM 480p" (VP8 / libvorbis, very slow) and
  offers "Ogg 480p" as a rendition. On this hardware the WebM VP8 encode
  of a normal broadcast clip runs past the platform's 600s command-line
  timeout and is killed with exit code 137, so the whole video-conversion
  Work fails and vid:transcodedVideos is never populated. The asset then
  shows "Processing..." forever and no poster thumbnail is generated
  (ThumbnailVideoFactory needs the picture:views poster frame that the
  same pipeline produces).

  MAM only needs ONE web-playable proxy, and the custom frontend
  (VideoPlayer.tsx) already prefers an MP4 (H.264) proxy. So this
  contribution keeps the fast MP4 conversion and disables the slow WebM
  and Ogg ones.

  Both AutomaticVideoConversion and VideoConversion are Nuxeo runtime
  Descriptors keyed by their `name` (getId() == name) with an `enabled`
  flag, so re-declaring an entry with the same name and enabled="false"
  merges over the stock one and switches it off. This requires this
  component to be contributed AFTER the stock
  org.nuxeo.ecm.platform.video.service.contrib, which the <require>
  below guarantees.
-->
<component name="com.mam.platform.core.video" version="1.0">

  <require>org.nuxeo.ecm.platform.video.service.contrib</require>

  <!-- Turn off the slow proxy transcodes at the automatic-conversion level
       so they never run on upload. Only MP4 480p stays automatic. -->
  <extension target="org.nuxeo.ecm.platform.video.service.VideoService"
    point="automaticVideoConversions">
    <automaticVideoConversion name="MP4 480p" order="0" enabled="true" />
    <automaticVideoConversion name="WebM 480p" enabled="false" />
    <automaticVideoConversion name="Ogg 480p" enabled="false" />
  </extension>

  <!-- Also drop the WebM/Ogg renditions so they are not offered on demand
       (they would hit the same slow-encode timeout). MP4 remains as the
       single web-playable rendition. -->
  <extension target="org.nuxeo.ecm.platform.video.service.VideoService"
    point="videoConversions">
    <videoConversion name="WebM 480p" converter="convertToWebM" height="480"
      rendition="true" enabled="false" />
    <videoConversion name="Ogg 480p" converter="convertToOgg" height="480"
      rendition="true" enabled="false" />
  </extension>

</component>
